WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.009
Here’s something that everyone at the SCP
Foundation knows: Portals to another world

00:00:05.009 --> 00:00:08.690
located in Indiana are incredibly bad news.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:14.799
The best example being SCP-2935, the limestone
cavern in Indiana that leads to a dimension

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:18.730
where all life has ended and Death reigns
supreme.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:23.310
So, considering the importance of keeping
things like this under control, we’ve decided

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:28.689
to fire up the Anom-O-Tron 6000 and simulate
sending one of the Foundation’s most reliable

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:35.960
senior researchers - Dr. Charles Ogden Gears
- to investigate another dimensional anomaly,

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:39.469
this time in a little town called Hawkins,
Indiana.

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:44.129
Can Dr. Gears in his younger years hold his
own against the Demogorgon, Demodogs, the

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:46.280
Mindflayer, and even Vecna himself?

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.260
Let’s fire up the machine and find out!

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.270
It was November of 1983, and Dr. Gears awoke
to a call on his home phone.

00:00:55.270 --> 00:01:00.300
Ordinarily, he liked to start his day with
a cold shower and a cup of plain black coffee,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:05.650
but on this particular very early morning,
he was yanked out of a lovely, dreamless sleep

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:09.120
by the sound of his superior at the SCP Foundation.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:10.120
"Gears.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.880
There's something strange going on in this
town in Indiana.

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:16.370
We're putting together a task force, and you're
going to lead it."

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.420
"What's been going on?"

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.680
"We don't know much yet, but there have been
reports of strange noises, unusual activity,

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.750
and a local kid's gone missing.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.380
That was all Dr. Gears needed to hear.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:27.970
"Alright, I'll start packing."

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:32.830
He placed the phone back in the receiver,
brewed himself that cup of coffee, hopped

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:38.450
in the shower, and filled a suitcase with
all of his usual necessities: flannel pajamas,

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:44.380
five white lab coats, plain slacks, and shirts,
and one pair of sensible shoes.

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:49.659
He dressed in an identical outfit to the ones
lining the inside of his slate grey suitcase,

00:01:49.659 --> 00:01:53.570
combed his hair, and straightened his tie,
and that was that.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:57.049
He was ready for whatever awaited him on this
new mission.

00:01:57.049 --> 00:02:01.610
When the official SCP Foundation-issued transportation
came to pick him up, one of the task force

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:06.480
members handed him a dossier, and a thermos
filled with more coffee, enough to sustain

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.630
him for the drive.

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:11.000
"So," Dr. Gears flipped open the file, taking
a look inside.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.100
"Where are we headed?"

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.000
"Don't know too much about it, sir."

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.000
The man shrugged.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.500
"Some little podunk place called Hawkins."

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:21.800
Dr. Gears spent the drive to Hawkins, Indiana,
looking over the few details the Foundation

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:23.340
knew so far.

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.819
Their interest had been piqued when a young
boy, Will Byers, disappeared mysteriously

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:30.310
on a bike ride home from a friend's house.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:34.370
In addition to the missing persons report,
townspeople had called the authorities to

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:39.269
complain about strange noises, and there were
rumors of a secret research project being

00:02:39.269 --> 00:02:42.489
conducted by the U.S. Government in the area.

00:02:42.489 --> 00:02:47.730
All of these factors combined to make Hawkins
a potential hotbed for anomalous activity,

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:52.460
and a place of significant interest to the
SCP Foundation.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:57.640
Dr. Gears would be tasked with setting up
a temporary Foundation site in town, disguised

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:02.569
as the headquarters of a new landscaping business,
and leading a group of researchers in the

00:03:02.569 --> 00:03:07.670
investigation of the Byers disappearance,
as well as cataloging other potential anomalies

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.390
present in the town.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:14.040
They were to remain there indefinitely, and,
to ensure their work would not be compromised,

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:19.280
they were given strict instructions not to
draw any unnecessary attention to themselves,

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:24.500
from civilians or operatives from any Government
organizations with an established presence

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.500
in the town.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:30.950
As Dr. Gears and his team rolled into the
town, he was struck by how completely, absolutely

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.550
ordinary it was.

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:37.860
They passed the town hall, the library, a
general store, a movie theatre, one sleepy

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:43.200
little pub packed with a few regulars, a hunting
and camping supply store, a few diversions

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.540
for the kids and young at heart like the arcade,
schools, all hallmarks of classic American

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:50.489
small-town normalcy.

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:55.050
As they drove out into the forest around the
town, however, away from the friendly veneer

00:03:55.050 --> 00:04:00.879
of suburbia, Dr. Gears spotted something unusual,
something he made a note of the second he

00:04:00.879 --> 00:04:05.830
caught a glimpse of it.There was a large,
official-looking building, surrounded by barbed

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:08.110
wire and armed military guards.

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:09.200
"What's that there?"

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.120
He asked one of his assistants.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.409
"Hawkins National Laboratory," she replied.

00:04:14.409 --> 00:04:17.360
"Says here they're under the jurisdiction
of the Department of Energy."

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:19.959
"Hm," was all he said.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:24.470
He would make sure to send someone out to
investigate once they were all settled properly.

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:28.370
After several years at the Foundation, he
had something of a sixth sense for detecting

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.970
things that didn't belong.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.710
This place...wasn't what it claimed to be.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:39.160
By nightfall, Dr. Gears and his team of six
officers had settled into their Foundation-provided

00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:42.400
housing, located across the street from their
front business.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:47.050
Privately, Dr. Gears hoped that the people
of Hawkins weren't especially interested in

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:48.180
landscaping.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:51.900
He didn't know a damn thing about hedges or
whatever else that job entailed.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:57.680
While the SCP Foundation maintained a steady,
quiet presence in Hawkins, the anomalous activity

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:58.920
only escalated.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:04.600
There were reports of a monster, a giant horrible
thing with a humanoid build and a face like

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:07.150
an open flower filled with teeth.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:11.750
Dr. Gears and four members of the team attempted
to track down one of these creatures, hoping

00:05:11.750 --> 00:05:17.759
to bring it into custody and study it up close,
and, outside of the home of the missing boy,

00:05:17.759 --> 00:05:20.770
they finally came face to face with the thing.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:26.130
The predatory creature was tall and thin,
with elongated limbs, ending in sharp claws.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:30.840
It reminded Dr. Gears a bit of an anomaly
he had seen in passing, though he had never

00:05:30.840 --> 00:05:33.070
seen that thing's face.

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:36.430
This beast, however, gave him an up close
and personal look.

00:05:36.430 --> 00:05:40.970
At first glance, its head looked like the
closed bud of a flower, with no discernible

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:41.970
features.

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:47.800
However, as it prepared to attack, letting
out an unearthly screech, fleshy petals unfurled,

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.240
revealing rows of razor-sharp teeth and a
gaping maw of a mouth.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:56.790
The officers opened fire immediately, but
the bullets did little to deter the advancing

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.790
creature.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.039
They only seemed to make it angry.

00:06:00.039 --> 00:06:03.710
Before they could apprehend the creature,
or, more likely, find themselves pulled into

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:08.850
its wide-open mouth, they were interrupted
by a group of surprisingly enterprising children

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.259
luring it away, seemingly to trap it.

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:15.470
Two teenage boys and a girl managed to light
the beast on fire, and send it retreating

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.690
back to wherever it came from.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:22.389
Dr. Gears and his men stayed out of sight,
as one of them remarked, "I guess the children

00:06:22.389 --> 00:06:23.710
really are our future."

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:28.139
Meanwhile, the other two officers were following
up on reports of a strange girl appearing

00:06:28.139 --> 00:06:30.070
in town as if from nowhere.

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:36.110
It was difficult to separate rumor from reality
amidst talk of secret government mind experiments,

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:41.010
roving gangs of children, and something to
do with Eggo waffles, but they managed to

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:44.150
trace the Person of Interest to the local
middle school.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:48.750
They arrived at the Middle School just in
time to watch the girl use apparent psychic

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:53.440
abilities to fend off government operatives,
before the same monster arrived to massacre

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:58.930
the men as the two operatives watched from
a distance, hidden just out of sight.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:03.530
They prepared to apprehend the monster and
administer amnestics to the children present,

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.430
but before they could, the girl and the monster
were gone.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:11.699
Shortly after this incident, Will Byers was
reportedly returned to his home.

00:07:11.699 --> 00:07:17.780
But Dr. Gears couldn't leave Hawkins just
yet, not with so many new questions unanswered.

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:19.910
Where had the Byers boy been all this time?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.720
What was the creature they had encountered?

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:24.229
Where had it come from?

00:07:24.229 --> 00:07:27.070
What had that unusually powerful girl done
with it?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:32.030
And, most importantly, would more follow in
the beast's footsteps, coming to snatch more

00:07:32.030 --> 00:07:33.950
children from the streets?

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:38.720
With authorization from the SCP Foundation,
Dr. Gears reached out to Dr. Owens at the

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:40.320
mysterious laboratory.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:44.750
He offered to share the information they had
managed to gather, if Dr. Owens would provide

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.410
him with full transparency and do the same.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:52.940
Owens was hesitant, but after being subjected
to one of Dr. Gears' trademark hour-long lectures

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:57.620
consisting of reasoned, logical, extremely
dry arguments, he relented.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.770
Dr. Gears celebrated this little triumph,
and Dr. Owens reported a persistent headache

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:06.690
after listening to the other man prattle on
for such a long time.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:12.360
Dr. Gears and his team now had concrete information
to share with their higher-ups at the Foundation.

00:08:12.360 --> 00:08:16.400
They learned all about the gateway to another
world that the scientists had opened at the

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:20.460
lab, the creatures that had come through its
supernatural doorway, and the connection to

00:08:20.460 --> 00:08:23.530
the psychic girl that had disappeared at the
Middle School.

00:08:23.530 --> 00:08:27.750
Now that an open line of communication had
been established, Dr. Gears was working to

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:33.410
convince Owens and the rest of the scientists
at the lab to allow him to use their portal.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:38.000
It was his intention to take his team of six
operatives through the gateway, into this

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.070
other world.

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:43.300
There, he would be able to create a first-hand
report for the Foundation, allowing them to

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:49.250
categorize the various creatures inside, and
perhaps the strange new dimension itself.

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:54.680
However, just after Dr. Owens and his staff
agreed to allow an SCP Foundation expedition

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:59.650
into the Upside Down, as it was colloquially
called, disaster struck.

00:08:59.650 --> 00:09:04.510
A presence from the other side of the gate
used the Byers boy to infiltrate the laboratory,

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:08.330
dispatching a group of juvenile creatures
to attack the scientists there.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:12.720
Dr. Gears was inside when it happened, looking
through some of the official reports he had

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:14.630
been granted access to.

00:09:14.630 --> 00:09:20.399
Suddenly, there were sounds of chaos from
down the hall, shrieks of terror and agony.

00:09:20.399 --> 00:09:24.560
He peered through the window of the room to
see quadrupedal, almost canine variations

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:29.510
on the larger monster bounding down the hallway,
leaving a trail of blood in their wake.

00:09:29.510 --> 00:09:34.560
Remembering his commitment to avoid involving
himself unless absolutely necessary, Dr. Gears

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.541
barricaded the door and hid from the creatures
as they ripped through the rest of the lab.

00:09:39.541 --> 00:09:44.980
The doglike monsters tore the lab staff apart
and injured Dr. Owens in the process.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:49.180
Then, in retaliation, the psychic girl closed
the gate between the worlds.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:54.170
In doing so, she removed the threat of the
monsters tearing Dr. Gears limb from limb

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:58.170
as they had so many others, but the damage
was done just the same.

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:03.040
If that wasn't bad enough, a tape of Dr. Owens
speaking candidly about the lab's activity

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:08.070
was leaked to the local media, and the laboratory
was promptly shut down for good.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:12.850
With it, it seemed all of the Foundation's
access to the anomalies in Hawkins were lost.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:17.100
Still, in spite of these new obstacles, Dr.
Gears refused to give up.

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:21.470
There were terribly strange things afoot in
Hawkins, and he had been sent there to uncover

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:22.470
them.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.930
He was going to continue to do his job until
some authority told him otherwise.

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:30.640
Besides, he had gotten quite used to living
undercover in this little town.

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.350
He didn't get out much, but he hadn't gotten
out all that much before Hawkins either.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:40.510
It was nice to settle into small-town life,
where very little ever changed...until the

00:10:40.510 --> 00:10:42.640
Starcourt Mall opened.

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:47.750
Local businesses began to close, disrupting
Dr. Gears' routine and causing him a great

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:49.140
deal of irritation.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:54.260
And then, of course, there was the matter
of the secret Russian laboratory beneath that

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:59.270
mall, which unleashed a malevolent entity
from the Upside Down into the town.

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:03.550
The Foundation team watched as, yet again,
the familiar group of civilians neutralized

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:07.310
the threat and closed the gateway to the other
world.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:11.420
Several of Dr. Gears' assistants suggested
interrogating the civilians, or at the very

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:15.070
least giving them amnestics to make them forget
what they had seen.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:19.870
Dr. Gears, ever the stickler for the rules,
reminded them that they had been given strict

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:22.050
orders not to interfere.

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:26.140
If the threat moved outside of the bounds
of Hawkins, that would be one thing.

00:11:26.140 --> 00:11:28.570
For now, it seemed fairly well-contained.

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:32.250
In fact, it seemed as if it all might be over
for good.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:37.940
The Byers family left town for California,
and life in town settled back into a mundane

00:11:37.940 --> 00:11:38.940
rhythm.

00:11:38.940 --> 00:11:41.260
Or, at least it did, until the murders began.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:45.209
First, a well-liked cheerleader, found mutilated
in a trailer.

00:11:45.209 --> 00:11:47.500
Then, an ambitious student reporter.

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:53.670
The town flew into chaos, blaming anything
they could think of for the horrific losses.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:58.690
Dungeons and Dragons, the misunderstood tabletop
roleplaying game, was a convenient scapegoat.

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:01.860
But of course, Dr. Gears knew better.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:07.480
This was the influence of something from the
other side, something not of this plane.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:12.350
If only he could get back through a gate,
and finally take a look for himself.

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:17.420
Dr. Gears was not a praying kind of man, but
his quiet wishes were answered when one of

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.890
his men returned to headquarters after taking
a swim in a nearby lake.

00:12:21.890 --> 00:12:25.160
He ran through the door, still sopping wet.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:26.300
"Sir!"

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:28.440
He panted, "You're gonna want to see this."

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:30.420
"Please get a towel first."

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:31.530
Dr. Gears insisted.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.339
"You're dripping all over the floor.

00:12:33.339 --> 00:12:35.360
It's hardwood; show some decency."

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.329
After the man was sufficiently dry, Dr. Gears
brought the team to investigate the lake.

00:12:40.329 --> 00:12:44.120
There, at the bottom of the water, was an
ominous red glow.

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:45.370
A gate.

00:12:45.370 --> 00:12:50.529
He couldn't be sure how, or why, it had opened
on its own down there, but an opportunity

00:12:50.529 --> 00:12:52.850
had finally presented itself.

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:56.839
He called his superiors at the Foundation,
suited up in protective gear complete with

00:12:56.839 --> 00:13:02.300
pistols and waterproof communication systems,
and dove down into the water, three officers

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:03.660
right behind him.

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:07.779
The other three would remain on the other
side, ready to call for backup, or swiftly

00:13:07.779 --> 00:13:10.720
flee town, if anything went sideways.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:15.050
Finally, Dr. Gears would lead an expedition
into the Upside Down.

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:19.540
As they swam toward the bottom of the lake,
into the gate to the unknown, writhing black

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:24.930
tendrils slithered out from the opening, snaking
around the three men accompanying him, and

00:13:24.930 --> 00:13:26.399
yanking them through.

00:13:26.399 --> 00:13:31.019
Dr. Gears was an excellent swimmer, the monotony
of laps in his local pool being one of his

00:13:31.019 --> 00:13:35.980
favorite ways to maintain top-notch physical
shape, and he sped through the water after

00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:36.980
them.

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:40.779
When he entered the gate, he suddenly emerged
into a dark facsimile of the world he had

00:13:40.779 --> 00:13:42.550
just left behind.

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:45.930
He peered through the visor of his suit, taking
in his surroundings.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:52.920
It was a cold, shadowy landscape, shaped vaguely
like Hawkins, but alien and foreboding.

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.209
More of those vine-like tentacles curled along
the ground, and gray spores drifted through

00:13:57.209 --> 00:13:59.170
the air like falling snow.

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:03.740
The cries of strange creatures filled the
air, drowned out only by...

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:08.080
The pained screams of the three men he had
followed through the gate!

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:11.630
Dr. Gears looked around for the source of
the sound, and spotted it: the three members

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:15.420
of personnel were struggling to free themselves
from the grip of the ropy tendrils that had

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:20.589
pulled them inside, and as they did, winged
creatures were descending on them from above,

00:14:20.589 --> 00:14:21.589
on all sides.

00:14:21.589 --> 00:14:28.470
They vaguely resembled bats, with flapping
leathery wings, but their faces, their mouths,

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:33.360
were completely unlike anything Dr. Gears
had ever seen, with the exception of the other

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:38.889
monsters that had crossed through the rift
from this place and into his own world.

00:14:38.889 --> 00:14:43.480
These bat-like creatures were swarming his
team, biting at their flesh as the men helplessly

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.160
tried to fend them off.

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:50.010
There was only one thing to do: Dr. Gears
drew his weapon and fired it into the sky

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.699
at the teeming mass of wings and teeth.

00:14:52.699 --> 00:14:55.890
The bat-things reacted and turned their attention
to him.

00:14:55.890 --> 00:15:00.100
His marksmanship did not miss, however, and
he managed to take out a dozen or so of the

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:04.031
vermin before his men could free themselves
and come to his aid.

00:15:04.031 --> 00:15:05.550
Two of his men, at least.

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:10.130
One, unfortunately, succumbed to his wounds,
and would have to be left behind.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.589
It was a shame, of course, but he knew what
he was signing up for when he joined the ranks

00:15:14.589 --> 00:15:15.810
of the Foundation.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:20.529
It was then that Dr. Gears remembered something
else he had brought with him, inspired by

00:15:20.529 --> 00:15:23.720
the victory he had witnessed all that time
ago.

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:29.079
The only thing that had sent the monster back
to hell was fire, so he had strapped a Foundation-issued

00:15:29.079 --> 00:15:30.690
flamethrower to his back.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:35.380
He drew this secondary weapon, a flamethrower,
and sent a blast of flame soaring through

00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:38.170
the air, barbecuing the bats to a crisp.

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:42.300
With the threat dispelled, at least temporarily,
he beckoned the men to follow him through

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:46.769
the unforgiving landscape, making note of
everything that he saw.

00:15:46.769 --> 00:15:52.220
For each and every detail that made Hawkins
memorable, there was an equivalent to it here,

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:55.910
covered in those strange spores and a layer
of palpable malice.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:16:00.470
As the group made their way through the Upside
Down, Dr. Gears at the front, they spotted

00:16:00.470 --> 00:16:05.490
what appeared to be the remains of the teenagers
whose deaths were being investigated in town.

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:09.290
They were bound up in the vines, left on display...but
by what?

00:16:09.290 --> 00:16:11.959
Or, more likely, by who?

00:16:11.959 --> 00:16:15.220
Dr. Gears could not see any other sign of
human life here.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:20.730
As his mind began to wander, running through
the possibilities, something caught his attention.

00:16:20.730 --> 00:16:25.410
A long, loud, clear sound, like the ringing
of church bells.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.020
No, not quite.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.170
Like the chime of a grandfather clock.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.950
It rang once.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:31.950
Twice.

00:16:31.950 --> 00:16:32.950
Three times.

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:33.950
A fourth.

00:16:33.950 --> 00:16:37.660
He couldn't see a clock anywhere, but the
sound appeared to be coming from a massive

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.630
house up ahead.

00:16:39.630 --> 00:16:44.300
Nestled within the trees, the eerie red light
just barely illuminated the place's silhouette.

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:49.110
But as Gears and his remaining two assistants
approached, he could see that it was a stately

00:16:49.110 --> 00:16:51.180
home, now in obvious disrepair.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:56.560
He had somehow missed its earthbound equivalent
and had never seen the place before.

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:01.220
But here it was, the door standing open, as
if beckoning him inside.

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.660
"Wait here, keep watch."

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:05.500
He nodded to the officers behind him.

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:06.689
"I'll take it from here."

00:17:06.689 --> 00:17:10.299
With his pistol in one hand, and the other
poised and ready to draw the flamethrower

00:17:10.299 --> 00:17:13.740
at a moment's notice, he stepped into the
house.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:16.000
He was right to have his weapon drawn.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:20.160
No sooner had he stepped inside than the vines
coiled around his ankles, one winding around

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.900
his throat and squeezing.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:27.439
With a few quick shots, he was able to force
them to recede, and continued his investigation.

00:17:27.439 --> 00:17:31.980
He climbed the creaky stairs to the attic,
looking for signs of new life.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:36.130
He briefly thought of trying to use his communicator
to check in with the men on the other side,

00:17:36.130 --> 00:17:39.400
but when he pressed its buttons, it only emitted
white noise.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:45.370
It was a favorite sound of his, one he vastly
preferred to the cacophony of music, but now

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.461
was not the time.

00:17:46.461 --> 00:17:48.950
He switched it back off, and carried on alone.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:53.360
Then, just as he crossed the threshold into
the attic, he heard it again.

00:17:53.360 --> 00:17:54.710
The chime of the clock.

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:59.740
In the corner of his eye, he spotted it, an
antique grandfather clock.

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:02.980
Before he could react to that, though, he
heard a voice behind him.

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:03.980
"Daddy?"

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.330
He turned to see a little girl staring up
at him.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:07.790
"Why are you leaving us?

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:08.970
Don't you love us?"

00:18:08.970 --> 00:18:10.559
He was too stunned to speak.

00:18:10.559 --> 00:18:15.530
The little girl's eyes turned white, her face
dripping like melting wax, as she repeated,

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.010
"Why did you leave?

00:18:17.010 --> 00:18:18.010
Why?

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:19.010
Why?

00:18:19.010 --> 00:18:20.010
Why?"

00:18:20.010 --> 00:18:22.540
He couldn't explain it, but his heart began
to pound, he could taste blood in the back

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.600
of his throat.

00:18:23.600 --> 00:18:29.580
Behind the little girl, a figure emerged,
human in shape only, a twisted face and form

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:34.930
made of exposed muscle and more of those awful
tentacle vines approaching him slowly.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:37.400
"It haunts you, doesn't it, doctor?

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:39.870
What you did to your family?"

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:42.830
the figure asked in a menacing voice.

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:45.630
Finally, Dr. Gears found the ability to speak
again.

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.570
"This all seems like a bit much.

00:18:47.570 --> 00:18:48.570
Don't you think?"

00:18:48.570 --> 00:18:53.490
He didn't have much patience for pageantry
of any kind, and he certainly didn't appreciate

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:54.490
this.

00:18:54.490 --> 00:18:57.060
"What is this...some sort of psionic mind
prison?"

00:18:57.060 --> 00:19:01.540
The entity that Dr. Gears had no name for,
but those determined kids from Hawkins knew

00:19:01.540 --> 00:19:05.010
as Vecna, tilted its head to the side quizzically.

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.890
"I can see your heart.

00:19:06.890 --> 00:19:10.500
I know the darkness within you," It hissed.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:15.130
Dr. Gears reached down for his communicator,
giving it one more shot as the entity approached

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:17.980
him with slow, threatening steps.

00:19:17.980 --> 00:19:22.580
As it reached its fingers toward his face,
he flipped a switch, and that lovely white

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.420
noise blared to life.

00:19:24.420 --> 00:19:27.210
Suddenly, the vision of the little girl was
gone.

00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:28.780
The clock stopped chiming.

00:19:28.780 --> 00:19:33.510
Vecna was still there, though, glowering at
Dr. Gears with a mixture of fury and just

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:34.670
plain irritation.

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:38.390
"I have more important things to attend to
than you.

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:41.450
Go back to your world...while you still can."

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:46.580
With a flick of his wrist, Vecna threw Dr.
Gears back down the stairs and out the front

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:50.400
door of the house, where his assistants were
still dutifully waiting.

00:19:50.400 --> 00:19:55.040
Dr. Gears was preparing to inform them of
his discovery, when he heard several new voices

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:58.090
in the distance, human and familiar.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:03.260
Those same children were back, once again,
seemingly to save the day as they had so many

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:04.340
times before.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:10.420
Ever the pragmatist, Dr. Gears brushed himself
off and headed back in the direction he came.

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:12.240
Best to stay out of their way.

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:16.740
Shortly after, Dr. Gears and his task force
withdrew from Hawkins, Indiana, returning

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:19.110
to their original Foundation Sites.

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:23.650
They could monitor the situation from afar,
and in the meantime, leave Hawkins to the

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:29.250
US Government, the Russians, and that constantly
surprising group of brave, clever civilians.

00:20:29.250 --> 00:20:33.430
Hell, maybe a few of them could be recruited
to join the Foundation when they got a bit

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:34.430
older.

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:38.250
When asked to submit an official report on
his findings in Hawkins, and his recommendation

00:20:38.250 --> 00:20:42.900
for how the Foundation should proceed with
the situation there, Dr. Gears simply wrote

00:20:42.900 --> 00:20:46.870
this: "To be completely honest, I think those
kids have got it covered."

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:53.870
Now go check out “SCP-096 VS Siren Head”
and “Could SCP-682 be Contained in the Backrooms?”

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.900
for more anomalous crossovers that are out
of this world!

